const embed = (id: string) => `https://iframe.mediadelivery.net/embed/776834/${id}?preload=false`;
const prose = 'mx-auto max-w-4xl px-6';
---

<Base
  title="Remote SDR Training | Get hired as a remote SDR from Nigeria"
  description="A step-by-step course that shows Nigerians how to get hired as a remote Sales Development Rep by a US, UK, or Canadian company, even with no sales experience. ₦60,000 for the first 100 students."
>
  <!-- Minimal header: logo + Student login only (no main nav) -->
  <header class="sticky top-0 z-40 border-b border-line bg-ivory/90 backdrop-blur-md">
    <div class="mx-auto flex max-w-7xl 2xl:max-w-[100rem] items-center justify-between gap-4 px-6 py-3.5">
      <a href="/" aria-label="Levi Henry Group home">
        <img src="/assets/brand/logo-horizontal.png" alt="Levi Henry Group" width="2232" height="955" class="h-8 w-auto sm:h-9" />
      </a>
      <a href="https://learn.thelevihenry.com/login" class="font-sans text-sm font-semibold text-navy underline-offset-4 hover:underline">Student login</a>
    </div>
  </header>

  <main id="main">
    <!-- Step 1: audience callout -->
    <div class="border-b border-beacon/30 bg-navy text-center">
      <p class="mx-auto max-w-5xl px-6 py-3.5 font-sans text-sm font-extrabold uppercase leading-snug tracking-[0.08em] text-white sm:text-[0.95rem]">
        <span class="text-beacon">Attention:</span> Nigerians who want to earn in dollars from home, as a remote sales development rep for companies in the US, UK, and Canada
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Step 2: headline + sub-headline -->
    <section class="hero-band relative overflow-hidden border-b border-line">
      <img src="/assets/brand/bg-hero-light.webp" alt="" aria-hidden="true" class="pointer-events-none absolute inset-0 h-full w-full object-cover opacity-70" style="object-position:right center" />
      <div class="pointer-events-none absolute inset-0" style="background:radial-gradient(70% 80% at 50% 40%, rgba(251,249,244,0.86), rgba(251,249,244,0.4) 55%, rgba(251,249,244,0.08) 100%)"></div>
      <div class="relative z-[1] mx-auto max-w-4xl px-6 py-14 text-center lg:py-20">
        <h1 class="font-serif text-[2.1rem] font-medium leading-[1.08] tracking-tight text-navy sm:text-4xl lg:text-5xl" data-reveal>
          Get hired as a remote SDR by a US, UK, or Canadian company, even if you've never worked in sales
        </h1>
        <p class="mx-auto mt-6 max-w-2xl text-lg leading-relaxed text-ink-soft" data-reveal>
          A step-by-step course that shows you exactly how to find the jobs, reach the hiring manager directly, call them, and win the interview you created. Built by an operator who went from no sales experience to top-performing SDR, Account Executive, and Sales Team Lead at a US CRM and AI company, working from Nigeria.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- The problem + what it's costing you (early agitation) -->
    <section class="border-t border-line bg-paper">
      <div class={`${prose} space-y-5 py-14 text-lg leading-relaxed text-ink-soft lg:py-16`}>
        <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl font-medium leading-tight tracking-tight text-navy sm:text-3xl" data-reveal>You've done everything you were told to do</h2>
        <p data-reveal>Maybe you've been searching for work for months and nothing comes back. Maybe you run a business, or sell online, and it just doesn't bring in enough, or often enough, to breathe. Maybe you do have a job, one of the ones that pays ₦150,000 to ₦350,000 a month, and you watch almost all of it vanish into transport and fuel that cost more every week. Or you earn less than that. Or, right now, nothing at all.</p>
        <p data-reveal>And Nigeria gets harder by the day. Working harder at the same things isn't moving you forward anymore. It's just keeping you in place while everything around you gets more expensive.</p>
        <p data-reveal>So you looked for a way out. You updated your CV. You applied for remote jobs on LinkedIn, Indeed, and every board you could find. Twenty applications. Fifty. Maybe more than a hundred.</p>
        <p data-reveal>And what came back? Silence. A few automated rejections. The occasional "we've decided to move forward with other candidates" from a company you're not even sure read your name.</p>
        <p data-reveal>Meanwhile, you watch people online talk about earning in dollars from home, working for companies in New York, London, and Toronto. It's real. You know it's real. But every door you knock on stays shut, and you start to wonder if it's meant for someone with a different passport, a different accent, or a different CV.</p>
        <p data-reveal>So you stay where you are, in the same squeeze, with family asking when things will change.</p>
        <p data-reveal>And here's what it's quietly costing you: every month this drags on, you fall further behind. The naira you earn buys less than it did last year, and less again the year after. People who started exactly where you are, who simply found the right door, are now earning in dollars and pulling away, while the window you keep telling yourself is still open gets a little smaller. The real price of staying stuck isn't only the money you're not making. It's the slow erosion of your belief that it was ever possible for you.</p>
        <p data-reveal>Here's the part nobody tells you: <strong class="font-semibold text-navy">the system you're using was never going to work.</strong> Hundreds of people apply for every remote role. Your CV is one PDF in a pile that a recruiter skims for six seconds. Applying harder just means getting ignored faster.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Step 2b: what's a remote SDR -->
    <section class="border-t border-line">
      <div class="py-14 lg:py-16">
        <div class={`${prose} space-y-5 text-lg leading-relaxed text-ink-soft`}>
          <p class="font-sans text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-navy-600" data-reveal>New to this?</p>
          <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl font-medium leading-tight tracking-tight text-navy sm:text-3xl" data-reveal>So, what's a remote SDR?</h2>
          <p data-reveal>An SDR, a <strong class="font-semibold text-navy">Sales Development Rep</strong>, is the first person on a sales team who reaches out to potential customers. You find the right company, start a conversation, and book a meeting for a senior salesperson to close. You don't close deals or touch anyone's money. Your job is to open the door.</p>
          <p data-reveal>It's the front door to tech sales for a reason. Companies hire SDRs for attitude, communication, and coachability, not for a degree or years of experience. The whole role is three skills you can learn: messaging on LinkedIn, writing emails, and talking on the phone. If you can hold a conversation and follow a process, you can do this.</p>
          <p data-reveal>And US, UK, and Canadian companies hire for it remotely, paying <strong class="font-semibold text-navy">$500 to $1,000+ a month in base pay, before commission</strong>, roughly ₦667,000 to ₦1.3 million a month, earned from your room in Nigeria. It's also where every sales career begins: today's SDR is tomorrow's Account Executive. It's exactly where I started.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Step 3: intrigue -->
    <section class="border-t border-line bg-paper">
      <div class="py-14 lg:py-16">
        <div class={prose} data-reveal>
          <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl font-medium leading-tight tracking-tight text-navy sm:text-3xl">Inside Remote SDR Training you'll discover</h2>
          <ul class="mt-6 space-y-3.5">
            {bullets.map((b) => (
              <li class="flex items-start gap-3 text-ink-soft">
                <svg class="mt-1 shrink-0 text-navy-600" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6" /></svg>
                <span set:html={b} />
              </li>
            ))}
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="mt-10 px-6" data-reveal>
          <EnrollButton course="remote-sdr-training" title="Remote SDR Training" ngn={60000} listNgn={80000} align="center" />
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Step 5: the solution -->
    <section class="border-t border-line bg-paper">
      <div class="py-14 lg:py-16">
        <div class={`${prose} space-y-5 text-lg leading-relaxed text-ink-soft`}>
          <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl font-medium leading-tight tracking-tight text-navy sm:text-3xl" data-reveal>The way in is to go to the decision-maker directly</h2>
          <p data-reveal>Remote SDR Training teaches you to get hired the same way SDRs win deals: <strong class="font-semibold text-navy">by going to the decision-maker directly.</strong></p>
          <p data-reveal>A Sales Development Rep's whole job is to find the right person at a company, start a conversation, and book a meeting. That's exactly how you'll land your role. You'll apply, then reach the hiring manager on LinkedIn, follow up by email, and pick up the phone. By the time you're interviewed, you've already shown them you can do the job.</p>
          <p data-reveal>It's 8 modules, in order, from your first LinkedIn message to the final interview.</p>
        </div>
        <ol class="mx-auto mt-8 max-w-4xl space-y-px overflow-hidden rounded-xl border border-line px-0" data-reveal>
          {modules.map(([t, d], i) => (
            <li class="flex gap-4 border-t border-line bg-paper-raised px-5 py-4 first:border-t-0 sm:px-6">
              <span class="font-serif text-xl font-medium leading-none text-brand">{String(i + 1).padStart(2, '0')}</span>
              <p class="text-[0.97rem] text-ink-soft"><strong class="font-semibold text-navy">{t}:</strong> {d}</p>
            </li>
          ))}
        </ol>
        <div class="mx-auto mt-6 max-w-4xl px-6" data-reveal>
          <div class="rounded-xl border border-line border-l-[3px] border-l-brand bg-paper-raised p-5 sm:p-6">
            <p class="font-serif text-lg font-medium text-navy">The course ends with a real shot at me.</p>
            <p class="mt-1.5 text-[0.97rem] leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">Your final assignment in Module 8 is to pitch yourself to me as an SDR for Levi Henry Group. Nail it and you earn a one-on-one discovery meeting with me, your shot to get in front of the person companies come to when they need sales talent.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="mt-10 px-6" data-reveal>
          <EnrollButton course="remote-sdr-training" title="Remote SDR Training" ngn={60000} listNgn={80000} align="center" />
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Step 6: credentials -->
    <section class="border-t border-line">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl 2xl:max-w-[100rem] px-6 py-14 lg:py-16">
        <div class="grid items-start gap-8 lg:grid-cols-[0.72fr_1.28fr] lg:gap-14">
          <figure class="m-0 overflow-hidden rounded-2xl bg-navy shadow-xl shadow-navy/25 ring-1 ring-navy/10" data-reveal>
            <img src="/assets/photos/headshot-editorial.webp" alt="Levi Henry, founder of Levi Henry Group and your coach" width="1280" height="1600" loading="lazy" class="aspect-[4/5] w-full object-cover" />
            <figcaption class="px-4 py-3 text-center">
              <span class="block font-sans text-sm font-semibold text-white">Levi Henry</span>
              <span class="block font-sans text-xs text-white/60">Your coach</span>
            </figcaption>
          </figure>
          <div class="space-y-5 text-lg leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
            <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl font-medium leading-tight tracking-tight text-navy sm:text-3xl" data-reveal>Why learn this from me?</h2>
            <p data-reveal>For fifteen years I've taught people to turn what they're good at into a living.</p>
            <p data-reveal>I started in Nigeria as a mixing engineer, producer, and songwriter. I worked with more than 1,000 artists and trained a generation of producers to build careers from their craft. Somewhere along the way I fell more in love with business than with the studio.</p>
            <p data-reveal>So I moved into sales, working remotely for companies in North America. I came in with <strong class="font-semibold text-navy">no B2B sales experience at all.</strong> What I had was what the studio taught me: how to run a business, how to read people, and the personality and confidence to sell myself.</p>
            <p data-reveal>That turned out to be enough to start. The system is what made it work.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-6" data-reveal>
        <p class="font-sans text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-navy-600">My path at Ivinex, a US CRM and AI company, fully remote from Nigeria</p>
        <div class="mt-5 space-y-px overflow-hidden rounded-xl border border-line">
          {path.map(([role, when, d]) => (
            <div class="grid gap-x-5 gap-y-1 border-t border-line bg-paper-raised px-5 py-4 first:border-t-0 sm:grid-cols-[auto_1fr] sm:px-6">
              <span class="font-sans text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-navy-600 sm:pt-1">{when}</span>
              <div>
                <p class="font-serif text-lg font-medium text-navy">{role}</p>
                <p class="mt-1 text-[0.97rem] text-ink-soft">{d}</p>
              </div>
            </div>
          ))}
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class={`${prose} mt-8 space-y-5 text-lg leading-relaxed text-ink-soft`}>
        <p data-reveal>Over that time I've led different groups of reps as people came and went, and taken teams from no results to strong results. It only happened after I'd produced those results myself first. That's the order this course follows: you do the reps, you get the results, then it compounds.</p>
        <p data-reveal>From a recording studio with no sales experience, to the top-performing rep, to leading the team, without leaving Nigeria. Everything in this course is what I actually did. I built Remote SDR Training to hand you that path, step by step, without the years of guessing.</p>
        <p class="font-serif text-xl text-navy" data-reveal>Talent is common. The systems that turn talent into income are rare. This course is the system.</p>
        <p data-reveal>Then, at the peak of it all, as Sales Team Lead, I walked away, to focus on training people like you reading this, and on building my business. Nobody believed I could make that kind of decision. I did it anyway. I make audacious moves, that's what got me into sales, and it's what made me the best.</p>
        <p class="font-serif text-xl text-navy" data-reveal>That's who I know you can become. Let me guide you.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="mx-auto mt-12 max-w-7xl 2xl:max-w-[100rem] px-6">
